WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:12.940
A British exit from Europe is the last thing
that Europe now needs, both from a political

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.860
and an economic point of view.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.750
Europe is still recovering from the great
economic recession.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:26.829
It hasn't yet attained the 2008 level of output;
its economy is weak.

00:00:26.829 --> 00:00:32.739
Britain would have to renegotiate terms not
only with Europe, but also with the rest of

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:35.079
the world in terms of their trade,

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:39.710
in terms of how their financial institutions
operate.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:45.089
From a political point of view, Europe doesn't
need this either, because what we see in Europe

00:00:45.089 --> 00:00:48.129
is we see Europe's politics fragmenting

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:52.940
we see a lot of populist movement, anti-European
sentiment.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:59.550
A British exit would really fan that kind
of sentiment, and that could lead to a fracturing

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.140
of Europe as a union.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.300
It could also lead to a renewed sovereign
debt crisis in Europe.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:13.540
My view is that Brexit could start the European
crisis anew.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:20.320
Please let us know your view in your comments,
and what other topics you'd like us to discuss

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.460
in 60 seconds on this and other issues.

